    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "TJ Gavigan are delighted to bring to the market this spacious four bedroom detached residence, beautifully positioned on extensive mature and landscaped grounds in the popular Bohermeen area.are delighted to bring to the market this spacious four bedroom detached residence, beautifully positioned on extensive mature and landscaped grounds in the popular Bohermeen area.\n\nOriginally constructed in the late 1980s, the property has been extended and upgraded over the years to create a substantial and comfortable family home. The accommodation is particularly generous, with three excellent reception areas, four bedrooms, two bathrooms and excellent storage throughout.\n\nThe property enjoys a wonderful private setting, approached through electric gates onto a sweeping tarmac driveway with ample parking. Mature trees, established hedging, extensive lawns and landscaped gardens surround the house, while a patio area provides an attractive outdoor entertaining space.\n\nA further benefit is the detached studio/granny flat, providing valuable additional accommodation suitable for a variety of uses, subject to any necessary planning requirements.\n\nThe gardens are exceptionally mature and private, comprising large lawns complemented by an excellent selection of established trees, shrubs and hedging. There is also an attractive patio area immediately adjoining the house.\n\nThe boundaries comprise a combination of walls, fencing and mature hedging, while exterior lantern lighting adds to the property`s attractive setting.\n\nA detached studio/granny flat and an additional garage provide excellent supplementary space. Set on C.1.06 acres/0.43 ha site, the property has site potential subject to planning permission.\n\nLocated in a peaceful rural area, within walking distance to local amenities in Bohermeen which include St.Ultans primary school, Bohermeen athletics club and Bohermeen Celtic football. Navan Town and the M3 Motorway are only a short drive from the property. Navan has a full range of amenities, including shops, schools, and leisure facilities. The M3 motorway is accessible C. 5.5 km from the property making Dublin only 45 minutes drive. It is an ideal family home for those seeking countryside living with excellent commuter convenience.\n\nEntrance Hall: 3.92m x 2.16m\nSpacious entrance hall providing a welcoming introduction to the property with built in storage\n\nSitting Room: 4.68m x 4.03m\nComfortable reception room with timber flooring and feature working open fireplace.\n\nKitchen: 4.12m x 3.15m\nBright fitted kitchen featuring an extensive range of timber units, generous worktop space, skylight providing excellent natural light and traditional range cooker. Archway through to dining room.\n\nDining Room: 4.24m x 4.03m\nSpacious dining area adjoining the kitchen with timber flooring and feature fireplace\n\nSun room: 6.68m x 4.63m\n\nA particularly impressive reception room overlooking the mature gardens. Featuring extensive glazing, timber flooring, recessed lighting, gas fire and French doors opening directly onto the patio and gardens.\n\nBack Hall:3.15m x 0.99m\nSpacious hall with built in storage and laundry facilities\n\nShower Room: 3.15m x 1.45m\nModern shower room with electric shower and contemporary sanitary ware and tiling.\n\nBedroom 1: 3.72m x 2.57m\nDouble bedroom with built-in storage\n\nBedroom 2: 2.63m x 2.85m\nBedroom with built-in storage.\n\nBedroom 3: 2.63m x 2.83m\nBedroom with built-in storage.\n\nBedroom 4: 3.15m x 3.04m\nDouble bedroom with built-in wardrobes overlooking the rear garden\n\nBathroom: 3.15m x 1.85m\nModern family bathroom with bath and contemporary tiling.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
